  "identity_adequacy": {
    "supported_rest_argument": "A gravity force kick raises kinetic energy before constraints cancel it; with no position motion and unchanged endpoint velocity, the measured staging term plus the independently measured constraint exchange equals the unchanged endpoint energy.",
    "free_fall_argument": "Force-boundary kinetic change and raw-potential position change are both retained, then the Rapier endpoint half-step projection is applied once. Their sum equals the endpoint-energy change of the same symplectic small-step trajectory without representing gravity as external physical work a second time.",
    "moving_vertical_argument": "Upward and downward initial velocity cross-terms cancel between force kinetic exchange and raw potential exchange, leaving the same integrator-specific defect and preserving signs before summation.",
    "zero_gravity_argument": "Zero gravity makes all three staging components and their signed sum exactly zero.",
    "sequence_argument": "Exactly sixteen contiguous source-measured small-step records prevent omitted, duplicated, stale, or reordered stage populations from being silently aggregated.",
    "binary64_control_operation_budget": 1024,
    "binary64_control_budget_provenance": "Sixty-four elementary binary64 operations per each of sixteen synthetic small steps bounds only analytic-control rounding accumulation; it is not an empirical margin, physical threshold, or runtime acceptance criterion.",
    "remaining_uncertainty": "This design does not prove that a native patch samples the declared boundaries, that a versioned engine-neutral ledger consumes the new channel, that the retained R49 candidate residual closes, or that recovery succeeds.",
